paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["EN4-URA-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Independently complete a substantial task on verse, prose and rhythm: produce an extended response or crafted piece (150–400 words as appropriate), embed evidence where relevant, and add a short craft reflection. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: original example using verse on new material; names a specific word, source or choice and explains its effect.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample error: Treating verse, prose and rhythm as personal taste only, or inventing details not in the text.. Correction: Strong answer: claim is arguable, evidence is precise, explanation links technique to effect.. Why it helps the audience is stated.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Treating verse, prose and rhythm as personal taste only, or inventing details not in the text. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating verse on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with verse, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept original work about verse with a specific supporting detail. Reject copied model wording with no new material. / Accept a misconception, a correction, and a purpose-linked reason for verse. Reject corrections that do not change the inaccurate idea..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for verse. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["claim is arguable, evidence is precise, explanation links technique to effect.","Treating verse, prose and rhythm as personal taste only, or inventing details not in the text.","Ignore the words and invent a more exciting event.","Skip the prompt because the first idea sounded good."],"question":"For verse, prose and rhythm, write claim–evidence–explanation in 4–6 sentences, or produce the required craft piece with one annotated technique. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"This is the misconception to avoid for verse; the other choices align with the lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Careful use of prose with clear evidence.","Treating verse, prose and rhythm as personal taste only, or inventing details not in the text.","Year 8 English develops reading and writing craft for verse, prose and rhythm.","claim is arguable, evidence is precise, explanation links technique to effect."],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with verse?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and a named prose, not by copying the model. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Apply verse to new material and name the prose used.","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence.","Treating verse, prose and rhythm as personal taste only, or inventing details not in the text.","Name prose only, without linking it to verse."],"question":"Which response best applies verse with new evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The skill is shown by quoting or pointing to wording that carries verse. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Say the writing is good without naming any words.","Treating verse, prose and rhythm as personal taste only, or inventing details not in the text.","Point to exact words in the sentence that show verse and s